## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical system design for regulatory compliance in multilingual content environments, focusing on per-language calibration, privacy preservation, and safe deployment strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual models with language-specific adapters
- Per-language risk calibration and drift detection mechanisms
- Privacy-preserving logging and active learning frameworks
- Gradual rollout, canary deployments, and automated rollback triggers

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo routing and scoring
function scoreContent(text) {
  const lang = detectLanguage(text);
  const adapter = getLanguageAdapter(lang);
  const riskScore = adapter.predict(text);
  return { language: lang, riskScore, decision: moderate(riskScore) };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design a practical, privacy-aware multilingual NLP pipeline with real-time latency constraints and governance mechanisms.

## Key Concepts
- **Multilingual encoders & per-language classifiers**: Shared XLM-RoBERTa backbone with lightweight task-specific heads per language
- **Latency budgeting**: Per-language SLA tracking (e.g., EN <100ms, DE <150ms)
- **Privacy by design**: Differential privacy-friendly logging, no raw data persistence
- **Drift detection & rollout**: Statistical monitoring with safe deployment/rollback strategies
- **Explainability**: Feature importance via gradient-based attribution

## Code Example
